<http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0401 ch13 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0401_ch13_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0401_page_data_v2_11_0.py from sen0401_ch13_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_CheckSoftwareDownload a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "How a user checks the downloaded software against the published list"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 13, The tarball hash matches: the SHA-256 of the tarball equals its line among the lines of SHA256SUMS and that line is in the saved copy of the list; a signature needs keys" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "TarballHashMatches" ; cme:accompanies "SignatureNeedsKeys" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a procedure with a decision - does the hash of the tarball equal its line in the list - and a different outcome on each branch: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_SecurityInSixBranches a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Bitcoin security in six branches"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 13, the whole chapter: the security model, protecting keys, keeping access, sharing control, custody history and survivability" ; cme:elementCount 23 ;
    cme:accompanies "SecurityModel" ; cme:accompanies "ProtectingKeys" ; cme:accompanies "KeepingAccess" ; cme:accompanies "SharingControl" ; cme:accompanies "CustodyHistory" ; cme:accompanies "Survivability" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter lays out one subject, Bitcoin security, by its parts: a topic and its parts"@en .
chx:Diagram_ColdSigningExchange a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A hot node and a cold node sign a PSBT without a blockchain on the cold side"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 13, A PSBT through a cold node: the cold node took the unsigned PSBT and returned a signed PSBT with the final witness, and the hot node finalized and broadcast it" ; cme:elementCount 4 ;
    cme:accompanies "PsbtThroughColdNode" ; cme:accompanies "WatchOnlyCannotSign" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between two nodes in an order that matters - the unsigned PSBT, the signed PSBT, the broadcast: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_HeirScriptLife a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The heir's coin, from locked to spendable after ten confirmations"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 13, The heir waits ten blocks: the heir's spend with sequence 10 was refused as non-BIP68-final at 1 and at 9 confirmations and accepted at 10, while the owner's spend was accepted at once" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "HeirWaitsTenBlocks" ; rdfs:comment "the passage describes the states a coin is in and the events that move it - refused at 1 and 9 confirmations, accepted at 10: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_KeyChoices a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What a single key and a 2-of-3 wallet each give an owner"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 13, The odds of loss and theft: one key alone is lost with 0.1 and stolen with 0.05; 2-of-3 is stuck with 0.028 and robbed with 0.00725" ; cme:elementCount 6 ;
    cme:accompanies "OddsOfLossAndTheft" ; cme:accompanies "TwoOfThreeSigning" ; rdfs:comment "the passage lists what different setups offer an owner, under different conditions: a set of uses by actors"@en .
